        <dc:title>Aspect-Based Sentiment Analysis of Indonesian YouTube Comments on Electric and Hybrid Vehicles Using IndoBERT and IndoRoBERTa</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>The global shift toward sustainable mobility has increased the adoption of Electric Vehicles (EVs) and Hybrid Vehicles (HVs) as alternatives to conventional fuel-based cars. In Indonesia, the government promotes this transition through tax incentives, purchase subsidies, and the expansion of charging infrastructure. Yet, public adoption remains limited due to concerns about cost, battery durability, and charging accessibility. This study applies Aspect-Based Sentiment Analysis (ABSA) using IndoBERT and IndoRoBERTa to analyze 37,407 Indonesian YouTube comments discussing EVs and HVs. After preprocessing and annotation, comments were categorized into predefined aspects—Performance and Driving, Cost and Economic Value, Features and Design, Battery and Charging System for EVs, and Hybrid System Component for HVs-and assigned a sentiment polarity label. Both models were fine-tuned and assessed using macro-averaged Precision, Recall, and F1-Score. IndoRoBERTa achieved the best performance, obtaining an F1-Score of 0.3319 on the HV dataset, indicating a stronger ability to interpret informal Indonesian expressions. Overall, comments about HVs reflected a higher proportion of positive sentiment (73.28%) than EVs (66.69%). Toyota and Honda were the most frequently mentioned hybrid brands, while Wuling and Hyundai dominated EV discussions. These results suggest that Indonesian users perceive hybrid vehicles as more practical and economically accessible. This study advances Indonesian-language ABSA research and provides insights to support policymakers and the automotive sector in strengthening sustainable mobility strategies.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2025-11</dc:date>
